From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Martin Lund <mrlund@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:10:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: do not tell peach the QDSS config is missing

With CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS in the host feature list, peach starts
initializing before the host has sent aux_ucode20.elf and the QDSS
trace config: both are refused with QMI error 90 (incompatible
state) and the firmware asserts in whal_aux_mac_trigger_wakeup.
Stock cnss2 sets the bit only when the QDSS file is missing, and
ROCKNIX's WCN7860 port (same PCI id) drops it for the same crash.
Without it (feature list 0x50) aux and QDSS are accepted and the
firmware reaches WMI ready; wlan0 registers.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
index 4fdb77480..098057eb2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/qmi.c
@@ -2356,6 +2356,14 @@ int ath12k_qmi_host_cap_send(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ab->id.device == 0x110e) {
 		req.feature_list_valid = 1;
 		req.feature_list |= BIT(6);
+		/* Peach must wait for the QDSS config before it starts
+		 * initializing. With QDSS_CFG_MISS set it starts at once,
+		 * rejects aux and qdss with err 90 (incompatible state) and
+		 * asserts in the aux MAC wakeup. Stock cnss2 sets the bit
+		 * only when the qdss file is missing. ROCKNIX's WCN7860
+		 * (same PCI id) drops it for the same crash.
+		 */
+		req.feature_list &= ~BIT_ULL(CNSS_QDSS_CFG_MISS_V01);
 		ath12k_info(ab, "qmi host feature list 0x%llx\n",
 			    req.feature_list);
 	}
